tt-toplike (0.7.25) noble; urgency=medium

  * Startup latency: the TUI painted its first frame ~1.3s after launch (and
    noticeably worse when a few instances started at once). The backend was
    being created and initialized up to THREE times before the first frame —
    once to auto-select in `main`, once in `run_with_backend`, and once more in
    `run_tui` (which owns the backend it actually uses) — and each Sysfs/Hybrid
    init shells out to `tt-smi` (~0.4s), so the wasted passes dominated boot and
    multiplied the `tt-smi` load under concurrency. The interactive path now
    routes straight to `run_tui`, which builds the backend exactly once; the
    per-backend construction in `main` is kept only for `--print`, and the
    `--remote` host-spec resolution is preserved. First paint drops to ~0.4s and
    stays flat when several instances start together.

