tt-toplike (0.7.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Animation FPS throttles: --throttle (load-based) and --idle-on-blur
    (focus-based), with /throttle and /idle-on-blur command-bar toggles and a
    status-bar hint. Both default off.
  * Apple Silicon host mode: --host now surfaces the GPU (utilisation + memory
    via ioreg) and Neural Engine (power via the private IOReport framework) as
    extra devices, no sudo required.
  * docs: mark --host and macOS/Windows builds as experimental; note the host
    mode observer effect (the visualiser shares the CPU it measures) and the
    per-hardware uniqueness of each device type, in README and project site.
  * Change: default log level is now Warn (was Info). This is global, not
    macOS-specific, so quieter startup output on Linux too; pass -v/--verbose
    for Debug-level logging, or -q/--quiet to silence entirely.

